# ADR 02 - How we build webapps

## Decision

- We use [Streamlit](https://streamlit.io/) to quickly develop dashboard MVPs. 
New dashboards can be deployed from our [Streamlit dashboard platform](https://github.com/ministryofjustice/coat-coh-dashboard/tree/main/dashboards).
- We use Python, with the [Flask](https://flask.palletsprojects.com/en/stable/) framework, follwing a backend-for-frontend architecture,
serving HTML/JS/CSS for production dashboards e.g. [CoPilot AI Credits Dashboard](https://github.com/ministryofjustice/moj-copilot-ai-credits-dashboard).

## Rationale

- Streamlit's pre-built React.js wrapper, allows for fast MVP development.
However, the wrapper presents limitations in terms of flexibility of frontend development, and potentially creates accessibility issues.
- Creating an entirely bespoke dashboard frontend, although potentially incurring a time cost,
offers superior flexibility when it comes to production dashboards.